1
00:00:00,643 --> 00:00:03,860
An invoice can pass a calculation check and still contain the wrong

2
00:00:03,895 --> 00:00:07,899
numbers I built Document Verification Lab to see what an independent

3
00:00:07,934 --> 00:00:11,742
visual check adds to document automation Start with this generated

4
00:00:11,777 --> 00:00:16,302
invoice and its payment details For a controlled stress test I multiply

5
00:00:16,337 --> 00:00:20,087
every amount by ten Subtotal shipping and tax still add up to

6
00:00:20,122 --> 00:00:24,277
the total so the arithmetic check passes Comparing the extracted values

7
00:00:24,312 --> 00:00:29,578
with the original page reveals the problem OpenBMB's MiniCPM OCR Jev

8
00:00:29,612 --> 00:00:33,142
takes the source image candidate text and a rendered copy of that

9
00:00:33,177 --> 00:00:37,726
text Its two-billion-parameter classifier returns a consistency score

10
00:00:37,761 --> 00:00:41,696
Higher means stronger predicted agreement with the pixels Here the score

11
00:00:41,731 --> 00:00:45,064
drops from about zero point nine eight to zero point zero zero

12
00:00:45,099 --> 00:00:48,987
seven I also ran real OCR on one hundred and twenty generated

13
00:00:49,022 --> 00:00:53,501
invoices Forty set the review threshold eighty were held out Rules

14
00:00:53,536 --> 00:00:57,540
caught all three test errors Adding the verifier sent thirteen correct

15
00:00:57,575 --> 00:01:01,418
results to review without catching another error The separate stress

16
00:01:01,453 --> 00:01:04,809
tests tell a different story All twenty-four internally consistent

17
00:01:04,844 --> 00:01:09,288
currency and amount changes passed the rules The visual verifier flagged

18
00:01:09,323 --> 00:01:13,084
every one That gives us a specific capability to investigate on

19
00:01:13,119 --> 00:01:17,147
representative documents For supplier-invoice workflows I would keep the

20
00:01:17,182 --> 00:01:21,163
source evidence attached measure the extra errors caught per review and

21
00:01:21,198 --> 00:01:24,913
check purchase orders separately You can inspect every case and change

22
00:01:24,948 --> 00:01:28,536
the threshold in the open lab The code inputs and results are

23
00:01:28,571 --> 00:01:29,311
public
